# CareFlow — environment template (Phase 0)
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored; ONLY this example file is tracked.
# NEVER paste real values into chat, issues, commits, or logs.
#
# Two separate hosted Supabase projects, both Mumbai (ap-south-1) — BUILD-SPEC.md §18.1, CLAUDE.md rule 12:
#   * dev  -> your local `.env`
#   * ci   -> GitHub Actions repository secrets, using the SAME variable names as below
# No Docker anywhere. Synthetic data only in both projects (`demo` profile) — no real patient data.
#
# Only keys needed for Phase 0 are listed. Keys for later services (LLMs, Qdrant, Langfuse, SMS,
# email, Gemini, ...) are added in the phase that introduces them — and per CLAUDE.md rule 13,
# only after you approve the service.

# ---- Environment ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which hosted project this file points at: dev | ci
CAREFLOW_ENV=dev

# Operating profile (BUILD-SPEC.md §2): demo | clinical. Use `demo` for dev and CI.
CAREFLOW_PROFILE=demo

# ---- Supabase project (Dashboard -> Project Settings) -----------------------------------------

# Project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co  (Settings -> API)
SUPABASE_URL=

# Public "anon" / publishable key (Settings -> API). Used only to sign test users in.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Service-role key (Settings -> API). SECRET, bypasses RLS.
# ONE-TIME SETUP ONLY (creating test accounts via the Auth admin API, BUILD-SPEC.md §21).
# Never used by the running app and never inside a test assertion. Leave blank in any
# environment that doesn't need to run setup.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# JWT verification (BUILD-SPEC.md Appendix B, open spike): the signing method of the hosted
# project is NOT yet confirmed. Fill in ONLY the one the spike shows your project uses; leave the
# other blank.
#   Asymmetric (JWKS): normally <SUPABASE_URL>/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json — leave blank to derive.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=
#   Shared secret (legacy HS256): Settings -> API -> JWT Secret. SECRET.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# ---- Database (Dashboard -> Connect) ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Format (SQLAlchemy async + asyncpg):
#   postgresql+asyncpg://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/postgres
#
# Which host/port to use is an OPEN SPIKE (Appendix B): the migration runner needs a
# session-level advisory lock, so it must NOT go through a transaction-mode pooler. Use the direct
# connection string, or the session-mode pooler if direct isn't reachable from your network
# (direct connections can be IPv6-only; note GitHub-hosted runners may lack IPv6 too — the spike
# will settle which string each of dev and CI uses). Do not use a transaction-mode pooler for
# the migrator.

# Migration owner / schema-changing role. Used ONLY by the migration runner. SECRET.
DATABASE_URL_MIGRATOR=

# Restricted application role (`careflow_app`, NOBYPASSRLS — created in task 2). This is what the
# API and the CI role-matrix/RLS tests connect as. SECRET. Never a superuser.
DATABASE_URL_APP=

# ---- App ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Allowed browser origin(s) for the API, comma-separated. Local Vite default shown.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
